    "editorial": {
      "title": "Malicious bee-js and Swarm Desktop releases abuse a trusted release path",
      "summary": "Socket and SafeDep report malicious @ethersphere/bee-js 13.3.0 and Swarm Desktop 0.56.2 releases delivering remote-code loaders. The npm package carried valid provenance; affected systems need compromise assessment, not just a package downgrade.",
      "why_it_matters": "Release provenance can faithfully attest to malicious code built through a compromised workflow. Swarm node wallet keys and persistent backdoors are part of the reported impact.",
